# mermaid.view: a diagram, drawn. The one view whose data is not fields but a SOURCE, handed to a
# renderer and printed as the text it comes back as.
#
# ONE way in, the decorator over the fence the forges already draw:
#
#   @{view:mermaid}
#   ```mermaid
#   flowchart TD
#       A[source] --> B{parse}
#       B -->|ok| C[render]
#       B -->|malforme| D[body]
#   ```
#
# WHY THE DECORATOR AND NOT A view:mermaid FENCE: the fallback. Where this hook does not run, in a
# reread transcript, on a forge, `view:mermaid` is an info string nothing recognises and the block
# prints as raw text, while a bare ```mermaid fence draws itself, the decorator line above it one
# harmless line of prose. This is the one carrier in the whole language whose fail-open is still a
# diagram, so it is the ONLY form: `@diagram` below makes the engine refuse the fenced block's flat
# data format outright (render.ts), and the payload rule refuses a table or a quote under the
# decorator the same way. The source arrives RAW under `content`, drawn by the engine, and the
# DRAWING is what gets neutralised: `A{{hexagon}}` is valid diagram source, not markup.
#
# The renderer is asked for its COLOURS, and this view is the one place in the language where that
# is not a message painting a terminal: a source naming a red box beside a green one is saying
# something about the GRAPH, and dropping it would lose meaning the author wrote, not decoration.
# So the drawing arrives painted, and NO tone is declared here: a tone would open a scope the
# drawing's own resets close on its first glyph, which reads as a tone that silently does nothing.
#
# NO CONTAINER, and it is the only view here without one. A box measures the value it holds as a
# SINGLE line, so a drawing handed to one comes back chopped every `width` columns, its own rows
# interleaved with the fold's. A diagram that wrapped would not be a narrower diagram, it would
# be a broken one. What a bare box bought elsewhere, this file buys by ENDING on its last row:
# no closing newline, or the file's own would print as a blank line under the drawing.
@diagram
${content}